    {
      "id": "def-effective-binary-encoding-and-decoder",
      "statement": "A binary encoding of a set $X$ is an injective function $e:X\\to\\mathbb B^*$. A total decoder for $e$ is a function $d:\\mathbb B^*\\to X\\cup\\{\\mathtt{mal}\\}$ such that $d(e(x))=x$ for every $x\\in X$. The encoding $e$ is effective when such a total decoder is specified.",
